The Q4_K mat-vec superblock loop is bottom-tested under an entry guard, which puts its body
in a block that dominates the loop exit and so brings it inside nir_opt_licm's reach.
nir_opt_licm.c's visit_cf_list calls visit_block only where current_block_dominates_exit
holds, so that a hoist never speculates; a top-tested loop reaches its successor through the
header's break, its body dominates nothing, and every loop-invariant value inside it stays
inside. At the pinned commit that is the pair of buffer descriptors: radv_nir_lower_descriptors
runs ahead of the LICM pass and emits their load at the use, so the body opens on
s_load_dwordx8 s[24:31] and an s_waitcnt lgkmcnt(0) ahead of its first vector load, and
depth.py records max_lgkm_in_flight 1 per iteration. The per-output-row block base
(s_mul_i32 and two s_add_u32 against first_row and num_blocks_per_row) is loop-invariant
for the same reason and stays inside for the same reason.

The guard reproduces the top-tested loop's iteration set exactly: both run the body for
i = ix, ix + it_size, ... while i < num_blocks_per_row, and both run it zero times where
ix is already at or past that bound. No arithmetic moves, so the accumulated value is
unchanged bit for bit.

Measured on the RADV RAVEN2 shim at the served shape, spec constants 0:64 1:4 2:1, over the
scale-word-select result this patch's preimage is: the loop body falls 365 to 349
instructions, its scalar count 20 to 4, and max_lgkm_in_flight 1 to 0, against 24 more
instructions across the whole shader, which is the entry guard, the bottom test, and the
hoisted values in the preheaders of the two call sites compute_outputs is inlined at. The
per-lane iteration count is ncols/1024 at BLOCK_SIZE 64, so the trade favours the hoist from
two iterations up. The two patches share the hunk region because both edit compute_outputs'
superblock loop, and the mechanisms are independent.
evidence/q4k-scale-decode/ carries the receipts and the appliance arms that remain unrun.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/mul_mat_vec_q4_k.comp b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/mul_mat_vec_q4_k.comp
index c3cf5ffb6..f14026a2e 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/mul_mat_vec_q4_k.comp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/mul_mat_vec_q4_k.comp
@@ -144,8 +144,19 @@ void compute_outputs(const uint32_t first_row, const uint32_t num_rows) {
     const uint scale_shift = 16u * v_im;
     const uint scale_shift_c = 16u - scale_shift;
 
-    [[unroll]] for (uint i = ix; i < num_blocks_per_row; i += it_size)
-        calc_superblock(a_offset, b_offset, v_im, scale_shift, scale_shift_c, q_offset, y_offset, i, num_blocks_per_row, first_row, num_rows);
+    // nir_opt_licm hoists only out of blocks that dominate the loop successor (nir_opt_licm.c,
+    // visit_cf_list), and a top-tested loop reaches its exit through the header break, so its
+    // body dominates nothing and every loop-invariant value inside it stays inside: the two
+    // buffer descriptors' s_load_dwordx8 and the s_waitcnt lgkmcnt(0) ahead of the iteration's
+    // first vector load among them. A bottom-tested loop under an entry guard puts the body in
+    // a block that does dominate the exit, over the same iteration set.
+    if (ix < num_blocks_per_row) {
+        uint i = ix;
+        do {
+            calc_superblock(a_offset, b_offset, v_im, scale_shift, scale_shift_c, q_offset, y_offset, i, num_blocks_per_row, first_row, num_rows);
+            i += it_size;
+        } while (i < num_blocks_per_row);
+    }
 
     reduce_result(temp, d_offset, first_row, num_rows, tid);
 }
